Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was a classic off-by-one error in `src/parse.py:4`. The function was using `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]` to get the first word from the split string. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because it returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error because there was no index 1 when splitting a single word

I fixed it by changing `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now all tests pass successfully.
